1
00:00:09,622 --> 00:00:14,085
KOCHIKAME

2
00:00:14,293 --> 00:00:17,130
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

3
00:00:17,338 --> 00:00:20,091
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, it's here&lt;/i&gt;

4
00:00:20,299 --> 00:00:23,136
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

5
00:00:23,344 --> 00:00:25,763
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, here it is!&lt;/i&gt;

6
00:00:25,972 --> 00:00:28,975
&lt;i&gt;Big waves, small waves,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny waves and middle-size waves&lt;/i&gt;

7
00:00:29,183 --> 00:00:31,644
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

8
00:00:31,853 --> 00:00:34,897
&lt;i&gt;Big boobs, small boobs,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny boobs and middle-size boobs&lt;/i&gt;

9
00:00:35,106 --> 00:00:37,900
&lt;i&gt;At the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle!&lt;/i&gt;

10
00:00:38,109 --> 00:00:40,903
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

11
00:00:41,112 --> 00:00:43,906
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived, it's here&lt;/i&gt;

12
00:00:44,115 --> 00:00:46,742
&lt;i&gt;Ah, summer's here again&lt;/i&gt;

13
00:00:46,951 --> 00:00:49,412
&lt;i&gt;It's come, it's arrived,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;it's here already!&lt;/i&gt;

14
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:52,665
&lt;i&gt;Big waves, small waves,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny waves and middle-size waves&lt;/i&gt;

15
00:00:52,874 --> 00:00:55,501
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

16
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:58,504
&lt;i&gt;Big butts, small butts,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;tiny butts and middle-size butts&lt;/i&gt;

17
00:00:58,713 --> 00:01:02,967
&lt;i&gt;At the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Bounce, bounce, bounce!&lt;/i&gt;

18
00:01:06,095 --> 00:01:15,438
&lt;i&gt;Here they come on the southern wind&lt;/i&gt;

19
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,986
&lt;i&gt;Bouncing at the beach&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Jiggling at the beach&lt;/i&gt;

20
00:01:23,321 --> 00:01:24,405
&lt;i&gt;Want you!&lt;/i&gt;

21
00:01:28,242 --> 00:01:34,040
LOTTERY GUY LUCKS OUT

22
00:01:34,248 --> 00:01:37,126
"KAME HALL PACHINKO"

23
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:40,797
Thank you very much.

24
00:01:41,005 --> 00:01:42,340
Please come again.

25
00:01:43,925 --> 00:01:47,678
I spent 20,000 yen in five hours on my valuable day off,

26
00:01:48,596 --> 00:01:50,932
and only won one cup of instant noodles!

27
00:01:51,140 --> 00:01:52,975
It's right before payday too.

28
00:01:53,184 --> 00:01:54,101
Dang it!

29
00:01:55,686 --> 00:01:57,814
I'm in luck this morning!

30
00:01:58,022 --> 00:01:58,856
What?

31
00:01:59,899 --> 00:02:02,360
Oh, you found some lost property?

32
00:02:02,568 --> 00:02:04,946
Thank you for your cooperation.

33
00:02:05,154 --> 00:02:06,489
You threw it away, didn't you?

34
00:02:07,114 --> 00:02:09,534
Lost property must be reported to the police.

35
00:02:09,742 --> 00:02:12,245
It's common sense in Japan, right?

36
00:02:12,912 --> 00:02:15,498
Come by the police station later for your 10% reward.

37
00:02:15,706 --> 00:02:17,750
It should be about one noodle.

38
00:02:20,545 --> 00:02:22,171
Why would I want that?

39
00:02:22,672 --> 00:02:25,299
That was close. I must survive until payday.

40
00:02:25,508 --> 00:02:28,678
Even one cup of instant noodles is a precious source of food.

41
00:02:30,805 --> 00:02:32,098
That's a loser too.

42
00:02:32,306 --> 00:02:33,224
Close though.

43
00:02:33,432 --> 00:02:35,226
Hey, what are you doing?

44
00:02:36,352 --> 00:02:38,229
We're checking the lottery numbers.

45
00:02:38,563 --> 00:02:41,065
The four of us bought 40 tickets.

46
00:02:42,984 --> 00:02:45,528
You shouldn't mess around during work hours.

47
00:02:45,736 --> 00:02:48,072
Why don't you talk about world affairs sometimes,

48
00:02:48,281 --> 00:02:50,491
like the peace process of Boston Hazelnuts?

49
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:52,326
Boston Hazelnuts?

50
00:02:52,535 --> 00:02:54,579
Don't you know, Chief?

51
00:02:54,787 --> 00:02:56,414
After Yugoslavia broke up...

52
00:02:56,622 --> 00:02:59,750
That's Bosnia and Herzegovina!

53
00:03:01,043 --> 00:03:05,172
You're always wasting time on gambling. So you have no right to criticize us!

54
00:03:07,717 --> 00:03:09,760
Playing the lottery is not gambling!

55
00:03:10,386 --> 00:03:12,513
Gambling tests your ability!

56
00:03:13,097 --> 00:03:15,975
You must achieve victory on your own.

57
00:03:16,183 --> 00:03:18,060
That is the way of the gambler!

58
00:03:18,269 --> 00:03:20,021
It's weirdly convincing.

59
00:03:20,646 --> 00:03:23,608
A book like that won't help you win big money!

60
00:03:23,816 --> 00:03:26,777
You have to invest time and money to make real dough.

61
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,904
Ignore him. Let's check the numbers.

62
00:03:29,113 --> 00:03:29,989
Yes, Chief.

63
00:03:30,406 --> 00:03:32,116
We have four tickets left.

64
00:03:32,533 --> 00:03:34,493
This one is... no good.

65
00:03:34,702 --> 00:03:37,079
You're going about it all wrong.

66
00:03:37,288 --> 00:03:38,706
You need to work up a sweat!

67
00:03:38,914 --> 00:03:40,082
Keep ignoring him.

68
00:03:41,918 --> 00:03:43,961
Oh well, all our tickets were losers.

69
00:03:44,754 --> 00:03:46,130
No wonder.

70
00:03:46,505 --> 00:03:51,761
Lady Luck won't smile on disrespectful guys like you.

71
00:03:52,803 --> 00:03:53,638
Hang on.

72
00:03:53,846 --> 00:03:56,182
I may have some tickets left from last year.

73
00:03:56,390 --> 00:03:57,642
Why don't you check them?

74
00:03:57,850 --> 00:04:00,561
This book has the winning numbers for each year.

75
00:04:00,770 --> 00:04:01,479
Good idea.

76
00:04:02,730 --> 00:04:03,814
I found one.

77
00:04:04,315 --> 00:04:09,153
What I hate most about the lottery is that winners hide the fact they won.

78
00:04:09,862 --> 00:04:14,659
&lt;i&gt;First prize, no. Second prize, no.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Third prize...&lt;/i&gt;

79
00:04:16,577 --> 00:04:20,998
&lt;i&gt;I won three million yen!&lt;/i&gt;

80
00:04:21,666 --> 00:04:25,169
In some countries the media announce the winners' names,

81
00:04:25,378 --> 00:04:27,755
but that doesn't happen here.

82
00:04:27,964 --> 00:04:30,508
That's because Japanese people are too stingy.

83
00:04:30,716 --> 00:04:31,884
Right, Chief?

84
00:04:33,010 --> 00:04:36,138
It's not right to hide it if you win the lottery, is it?

85
00:04:36,347 --> 00:04:37,807
Y-Yes, I agree.

86
00:04:38,391 --> 00:04:41,394
But people who play pachinko or bet on horses are honest.

87
00:04:41,602 --> 00:04:44,605
They show their emotions openly, win or lose.

88
00:04:44,814 --> 00:04:47,775
Ryo-chan, you lost at pachinko today, didn't you?

89
00:04:48,442 --> 00:04:51,362
Shut up! The outcome is down to luck!

90
00:04:51,570 --> 00:04:52,571
Chief.

91
00:04:53,656 --> 00:04:55,449
How did your ticket do?

92
00:04:56,742 --> 00:04:59,203
Oh, it was a loser.

93
00:04:59,412 --> 00:05:00,996
Never mind the lottery,

94
00:05:01,205 --> 00:05:04,083
let's talk about Bosnia and Herzegovina.

95
00:05:05,918 --> 00:05:09,505
Chief, are you hiding something?

96
00:05:09,714 --> 00:05:11,424
Nothing in particular.

97
00:05:11,632 --> 00:05:13,509
Are you sure?

98
00:05:14,593 --> 00:05:17,430
Hmm, it says here that when people win...

99
00:05:17,638 --> 00:05:23,018
"First, they suddenly become silent and distant."

100
00:05:24,562 --> 00:05:29,442
"Second, they change the subject and stop talking about the lottery."

101
00:05:30,568 --> 00:05:33,237
Chief, please show us your lottery ticket.

102
00:05:33,446 --> 00:05:34,947
It's a loser!

103
00:05:35,156 --> 00:05:37,241
Then, why don't you show us?

104
00:05:37,450 --> 00:05:39,618
No way! I won't!

105
00:05:39,827 --> 00:05:40,870
Stop it!

106
00:05:43,414 --> 00:05:44,999
Why are you so riled up?

107
00:05:45,207 --> 00:05:46,500
I'm not!

108
00:05:46,709 --> 00:05:49,170
I told you it was a loser!

109
00:05:49,378 --> 00:05:50,796
I checked the number myself.

110
00:05:51,005 --> 00:05:52,548
He looks really riled up.

111
00:05:52,757 --> 00:05:54,800
Huh? No, I'm not...

112
00:05:55,009 --> 00:05:58,596
-Tear the ticket up then. -What?

113
00:05:59,221 --> 00:06:02,850
It's just a loser, right? Here, I'll tear it up for you.

114
00:06:03,476 --> 00:06:07,438
No, thanks. I collect losing tickets.

115
00:06:08,230 --> 00:06:10,483
When did you start doing that?

116
00:06:10,691 --> 00:06:13,527
You have lying eyes. Show me that ticket!

117
00:06:13,736 --> 00:06:14,612
No!

118
00:06:14,820 --> 00:06:17,865
Get off! You'll tear it!

119
00:06:18,073 --> 00:06:20,201
Stop, you idiot!

120
00:06:22,161 --> 00:06:23,954
-Are you okay? -Ryotsu!

121
00:06:24,497 --> 00:06:29,001
Ouch. He wouldn't go so far for just 100,000 or 200,000 yen.

122
00:06:29,627 --> 00:06:31,754
He must've won a tidy sum!

123
00:06:32,546 --> 00:06:33,923
Terai, check the book!

124
00:06:34,131 --> 00:06:35,007
Got it!

125
00:06:35,883 --> 00:06:37,760
Which lottery is his ticket for?

126
00:06:37,968 --> 00:06:40,387
It's the same as this year, so...

127
00:06:42,890 --> 00:06:43,891
I found it!

128
00:06:44,099 --> 00:06:44,934
Good!

129
00:06:45,142 --> 00:06:47,603
Read out the prize money from the bottom.

130
00:06:47,812 --> 00:06:48,646
All right.

131
00:06:49,146 --> 00:06:51,357
Fifth prize, 500,000 yen.

132
00:06:53,359 --> 00:06:54,485
No.

133
00:06:55,027 --> 00:06:57,571
Fourth prize, one million yen.

134
00:07:00,407 --> 00:07:01,992
Not this one either. Next.

135
00:07:02,493 --> 00:07:03,744
Third prize, three million yen.

136
00:07:09,333 --> 00:07:12,503
That's it! He won three million yen!

137
00:07:13,087 --> 00:07:14,213
N-No!

138
00:07:15,422 --> 00:07:18,384
A small-minded person like you shows the truth on your face.

139
00:07:18,592 --> 00:07:19,969
You won the third prize!

140
00:07:20,636 --> 00:07:22,429
No, it was a loser!

141
00:07:22,638 --> 00:07:27,184
Winners of over one million yen are strictly checked by banks.

142
00:07:27,393 --> 00:07:29,979
That ticket is due to expire today.

143
00:07:30,855 --> 00:07:34,525
So today is the last day that you can go and collect the money.

144
00:07:42,032 --> 00:07:46,787
Chief, let's go drinking tonight until midnight.

145
00:07:48,247 --> 00:07:51,959
I'm sorry. I did actually win three million yen.

146
00:07:52,167 --> 00:07:53,794
Congratulations, Chief!

147
00:07:54,003 --> 00:07:57,590
You did nothing wrong, so you didn't have to hide it.

148
00:07:57,798 --> 00:07:59,758
Yes, I know, but...

149
00:08:00,176 --> 00:08:03,470
Not showing your emotions is a bad habit of Japanese people.

150
00:08:03,679 --> 00:08:04,513
Jeez!

151
00:08:05,222 --> 00:08:08,934
We should express joy with our whole body like people overseas do.

152
00:08:09,143 --> 00:08:12,980
Oh, I'm happy! I won the lottery!

153
00:08:13,188 --> 00:08:14,648
So happy!

154
00:08:14,857 --> 00:08:16,025
Goddamn!

155
00:08:16,233 --> 00:08:18,193
Give me chocolate!

156
00:08:21,530 --> 00:08:25,200
See? That's how you should express joy.

157
00:08:25,409 --> 00:08:26,410
You got it?

158
00:08:26,619 --> 00:08:27,995
Nobody anywhere does that.

159
00:08:28,829 --> 00:08:31,749
Let's call HQ and let everyone know about it.

160
00:08:32,708 --> 00:08:33,876
Hey, stop it!

161
00:08:34,084 --> 00:08:37,796
You only found out you won because you happened to check the book.

162
00:08:38,005 --> 00:08:39,465
It's like a hole in one in golf.

163
00:08:39,673 --> 00:08:43,510
The right thing to do is have a party and all celebrate together.

164
00:08:43,719 --> 00:08:44,887
But...

165
00:08:45,095 --> 00:08:49,058
Or were you going to keep the three million for yourself?

166
00:08:49,266 --> 00:08:52,061
No, I would never do that.

167
00:08:52,269 --> 00:08:54,188
Leave things to me then.

168
00:08:55,439 --> 00:08:57,900
This is Ryotsu at Kameari Park Police Station.

169
00:08:58,108 --> 00:09:00,152
We'd like a room for 200 people tonight.

170
00:09:00,361 --> 00:09:02,655
Please prepare some top-grade shabu-shabu.

171
00:09:03,197 --> 00:09:05,783
Shabu-shabu?

172
00:09:06,742 --> 00:09:07,576
Come on!

173
00:09:07,785 --> 00:09:08,619
Thank you.

174
00:09:09,244 --> 00:09:11,664
I'll go to HQ to tell them.

175
00:09:11,872 --> 00:09:12,957
Ryotsu!

176
00:09:13,499 --> 00:09:16,460
You were lucky to win the lottery...

177
00:09:16,669 --> 00:09:19,964
...but unlucky that Ryo-chan was here.

178
00:09:24,051 --> 00:09:27,471
A FEW DAYS LATER

179
00:09:29,098 --> 00:09:31,475
The chief seems to be off again today.

180
00:09:32,142 --> 00:09:34,937
He hasn't come in since that day.

181
00:09:35,145 --> 00:09:37,064
He should have recovered by now.

182
00:09:37,272 --> 00:09:38,983
He did look pretty shocked.

183
00:09:39,441 --> 00:09:41,443
Ryotsu went too far as well.

184
00:09:41,652 --> 00:09:45,531
Shabu-shabu was enough. There was no need for seven after parties.

185
00:09:45,739 --> 00:09:47,741
The chief has come!

186
00:09:52,287 --> 00:09:54,415
G-Good morning, sir.

187
00:09:54,623 --> 00:09:56,417
I'm sorry for causing you trouble.

188
00:09:57,126 --> 00:10:01,338
So, how much did it cost for those parties?

189
00:10:01,964 --> 00:10:04,091
Not a penny was left.

190
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:07,219
Please don't talk about it anymore.

191
00:10:07,428 --> 00:10:08,804
I'll get a fever again.

192
00:10:09,013 --> 00:10:14,184
That aside, Ryotsu has gotten hooked on the lottery since then.

193
00:10:14,393 --> 00:10:16,937
-What? -He's playing the American lotto.

194
00:10:17,146 --> 00:10:17,980
What's that?

195
00:10:19,273 --> 00:10:23,652
You pick six numbers from 1 to 51 and you win if they all get drawn.

196
00:10:23,861 --> 00:10:26,447
I heard the prize money is 5.5 billion yen.

197
00:10:26,739 --> 00:10:29,867
5.5 billion yen!

198
00:10:33,537 --> 00:10:37,041
No wonder Ryotsu has gotten hooked.

199
00:10:37,249 --> 00:10:39,543
But it doesn't sound easy to win.

200
00:10:40,169 --> 00:10:42,921
Ryo-chan says there must be some kind of pattern.

201
00:10:43,130 --> 00:10:45,007
He's collected data for the last five years,

202
00:10:45,215 --> 00:10:49,303
and went to see a mathematician to study promising combinations.

203
00:10:49,928 --> 00:10:51,847
He's so dedicated outside of work.

204
00:10:52,056 --> 00:10:52,890
Hello!

205
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:55,559
You're back, Chief.

206
00:10:55,768 --> 00:10:56,769
You fool!

207
00:10:56,977 --> 00:11:01,065
After mocking lotteries, you're apparently playing them a lot.

208
00:11:01,273 --> 00:11:02,775
Come on. Be more flexible.

209
00:11:02,983 --> 00:11:05,360
No matter what you say, 5.5 billion yen is at stake.

210
00:11:05,903 --> 00:11:08,614
Ryo-san, you have some notice letters from overseas.

211
00:11:08,822 --> 00:11:12,117
All right. I won't stop entering until I win.

212
00:11:12,868 --> 00:11:16,497
Won't you join me for the 5.5 billion dream?

213
00:11:16,955 --> 00:11:18,165
No, thanks.

214
00:11:18,957 --> 00:11:23,420
I guess you guys can keep chasing your modest dreams here in Japan.

215
00:11:23,629 --> 00:11:25,881
Right, let's check the results.

216
00:11:26,090 --> 00:11:28,467
The latest winning numbers are...

217
00:11:29,134 --> 00:11:31,845
2, 16, 17...

218
00:11:32,304 --> 00:11:34,807
Oh, the first three are the same!

219
00:11:35,015 --> 00:11:38,143
Next, 23, 34...

220
00:11:38,352 --> 00:11:40,521
Also the same!

221
00:11:40,729 --> 00:11:46,402
They must be trying to get my hopes up, then let me down on the last one.

222
00:11:46,610 --> 00:11:48,153
There, I knew it.

223
00:11:48,362 --> 00:11:50,697
If it was baccarat, I would've had the best hand!

224
00:11:50,906 --> 00:11:54,910
Damn it! Why did I pick four-five, instead of 45?

225
00:11:55,953 --> 00:11:57,788
Wait... Four-five?

226
00:11:58,664 --> 00:12:00,082
&lt;i&gt;But that's...&lt;/i&gt;

227
00:12:01,458 --> 00:12:02,417
&lt;i&gt;45.&lt;/i&gt;

228
00:12:09,967 --> 00:12:11,635
&lt;i&gt;Bingo.&lt;/i&gt;

229
00:12:12,136 --> 00:12:16,098
&lt;i&gt;I won 5.5 billion yen.&lt;/i&gt;

230
00:12:25,357 --> 00:12:27,484
&lt;i&gt;I won.&lt;/i&gt;

231
00:12:28,402 --> 00:12:31,405
Anyway, the lotto is amazing.

232
00:12:31,613 --> 00:12:34,408
Its top prize is 5.5 billion yen.

233
00:12:34,616 --> 00:12:36,451
-Right, Ryotsu? -Yeep!

234
00:12:37,161 --> 00:12:39,663
Did you say something?

235
00:12:42,458 --> 00:12:44,501
What's wrong? You look pale.

236
00:12:45,127 --> 00:12:47,463
I might have caught a cold while sleeping.

237
00:12:47,671 --> 00:12:48,672
I'm a bit feverish.

238
00:12:48,881 --> 00:12:50,757
How about your lotto results?

239
00:12:50,966 --> 00:12:52,885
What are you talking about?

240
00:12:53,385 --> 00:12:56,680
You were checking the winning numbers.

241
00:12:56,889 --> 00:12:58,348
Yikes!

242
00:12:58,557 --> 00:13:03,979
Instead, why don't we discuss changes to the consumption tax?

243
00:13:04,813 --> 00:13:09,067
Let's see, when people win...

244
00:13:09,276 --> 00:13:12,196
"they change the subject and stop talking about the lottery."

245
00:13:13,614 --> 00:13:16,033
How did you do in the lotto, Ryotsu?

246
00:13:16,241 --> 00:13:18,827
Let's put that aside.

247
00:13:19,203 --> 00:13:23,207
I'm on duty, so please don't talk to me for a while.

248
00:13:23,415 --> 00:13:27,336
And "they suddenly become silent and distant."

249
00:13:28,170 --> 00:13:29,504
C-Come on.

250
00:13:29,713 --> 00:13:32,549
I'm a man of few words by nature.

251
00:13:39,014 --> 00:13:40,682
You won, didn't you?

252
00:13:41,266 --> 00:13:43,268
What do you mean?

253
00:13:45,103 --> 00:13:47,648
Don't act stupid! I know you won!

254
00:13:47,856 --> 00:13:49,608
Won what?

255
00:13:49,816 --> 00:13:52,069
The lotto, of course!

256
00:13:52,277 --> 00:13:56,073
You won 5.5 billion yen, didn't you?

257
00:13:57,157 --> 00:13:58,909
I have no idea.

258
00:13:59,117 --> 00:14:02,663
He won. The winning numbers are identical to his picks.

259
00:14:03,622 --> 00:14:05,165
Hey, Nakagawa!

260
00:14:05,499 --> 00:14:07,918
You took notes. How dirty!

261
00:14:08,752 --> 00:14:11,672
Because we came up with the numbers together!

262
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:13,298
Stop, Ryo-chan!

263
00:14:13,507 --> 00:14:17,970
You really won 5.5 billion yen, didn't you?

264
00:14:18,303 --> 00:14:19,263
What?

265
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:21,431
You won, didn't you?

266
00:14:25,060 --> 00:14:25,936
Yes.

267
00:14:26,478 --> 00:14:30,440
After all you said about expressing joy like people overseas!

268
00:14:30,649 --> 00:14:33,277
You really are a small-minded person.

269
00:14:34,778 --> 00:14:36,613
Don't get me wrong.

270
00:14:36,822 --> 00:14:39,449
I am going to express my joy just like I said.

271
00:14:40,575 --> 00:14:41,410
Here I go.

272
00:14:41,868 --> 00:14:46,915
Oh, I'm so happy! I won 5.5 billion yen!

273
00:14:47,124 --> 00:14:49,459
Great! Goddamn!

274
00:14:49,668 --> 00:14:51,420
Give me chocolate!

275
00:14:51,628 --> 00:14:54,589
He's pretty laid-back for a guy who just won 5.5 billion.

276
00:14:54,798 --> 00:14:56,383
He's not. Look.

277
00:14:56,591 --> 00:14:57,968
His steps are very clumsy.

278
00:14:58,468 --> 00:15:01,680
Oh, I'm happy to win 5.5 billion!

279
00:15:01,888 --> 00:15:04,349
Give me chocolate!

280
00:15:09,604 --> 00:15:12,316
He's not really good at hiding his shock.

281
00:15:12,524 --> 00:15:14,818
He should just act happy in a normal way.

282
00:15:15,027 --> 00:15:17,487
Let's inform the media.

283
00:15:18,739 --> 00:15:20,824
Wait, please!

284
00:15:23,076 --> 00:15:27,539
You said we should tell everyone and celebrate, Ryotsu.

285
00:15:28,665 --> 00:15:30,667
Yes, I did.

286
00:15:31,168 --> 00:15:34,671
Please tell everyone in Japan.

287
00:15:34,880 --> 00:15:38,050
Hello, this is Kameari Park Police Station.

288
00:15:38,258 --> 00:15:41,595
This is going to be a big mess from tomorrow.

289
00:15:44,806 --> 00:15:45,807
"POLICE OFFICER GETS SUPER RICH"

290
00:15:46,016 --> 00:15:47,184
"WINS 5.5 BILLION YEN"

291
00:15:49,061 --> 00:15:50,520
Officer Ryotsu!

292
00:15:51,396 --> 00:15:53,648
You've become a star overnight.

293
00:15:53,857 --> 00:15:57,819
You wouldn't find it funny if it happened to you!

294
00:15:58,403 --> 00:16:00,447
You've got lots of letters from strangers.

295
00:16:00,656 --> 00:16:01,615
What?

296
00:16:02,449 --> 00:16:05,243
From "M. K." in Chiba Prefecture.

297
00:16:05,452 --> 00:16:08,413
"You got 5.5 billion yen all to your damn self.

298
00:16:08,622 --> 00:16:10,582
I bet you don't use it wisely.

299
00:16:10,791 --> 00:16:13,752
Go to hell, you bastard!"

300
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:15,337
Cut it out!

301
00:16:20,384 --> 00:16:22,427
Coming through!

302
00:16:25,305 --> 00:16:27,224
Komachi and Naoko?

303
00:16:27,432 --> 00:16:29,518
Lord Ryotsu, please marry me!

304
00:16:29,726 --> 00:16:32,229
I've always adored you, Lord Ryotsu!

305
00:16:33,063 --> 00:16:34,398
"Lord Ryotsu"?

306
00:16:37,275 --> 00:16:40,278
I knew you'd do something big one day.

307
00:16:40,487 --> 00:16:43,865
I want to hold our wedding ceremony straight away.

308
00:16:44,491 --> 00:16:45,951
Wait a second, Komachi.

309
00:16:46,159 --> 00:16:47,744
What, Naoko?

310
00:16:47,953 --> 00:16:50,372
I'm the one who's marrying him!

311
00:16:50,914 --> 00:16:55,210
He was the least eligible bachelor in the police department until yesterday.

312
00:16:55,419 --> 00:16:56,378
Shut up!

313
00:16:56,586 --> 00:17:00,382
I'd rather dump all the money in a ditch than marry you!

314
00:17:00,590 --> 00:17:01,716
Excuse me?

315
00:17:01,925 --> 00:17:04,219
That's so rude!

316
00:17:06,054 --> 00:17:08,181
Hey, Ryotsu. Do something!

317
00:17:08,390 --> 00:17:09,266
Chief.

318
00:17:09,474 --> 00:17:12,602
This fuss won't settle until you go outside!

319
00:17:13,019 --> 00:17:14,438
Damn it!

320
00:17:14,771 --> 00:17:15,605
Stop!

321
00:17:15,814 --> 00:17:16,982
Go away!

322
00:17:21,653 --> 00:17:24,990
I can't say anything, because I haven't received the money yet.

323
00:17:25,198 --> 00:17:26,700
-But you must... -Don't make excuses!

324
00:17:27,033 --> 00:17:29,870
That's enough!

325
00:17:30,954 --> 00:17:34,624
After I get the money, I'll tell you how I'll spend it and answer any questions.

326
00:17:35,250 --> 00:17:36,960
Until then, go home!

327
00:17:37,169 --> 00:17:39,463
So long! Goodbye! Farewell!

328
00:17:42,007 --> 00:17:44,384
A FEW DAYS LATER

329
00:17:44,843 --> 00:17:46,678
Yes, aha.

330
00:17:46,887 --> 00:17:48,638
Okay, I got it.

331
00:17:49,848 --> 00:17:50,807
What's up?

332
00:17:51,183 --> 00:17:53,435
My money was transferred from America.

333
00:17:53,643 --> 00:17:55,479
All 5.5 billion...?

334
00:17:55,729 --> 00:17:57,147
Shhh!

335
00:17:57,355 --> 00:18:00,358
Keep it down. The media might be listening!

336
00:18:00,567 --> 00:18:02,027
You don't want them to know?

337
00:18:02,235 --> 00:18:05,572
Of course not. I'll go get the money. You take care of things here.

338
00:18:18,168 --> 00:18:20,587
We've arrived, sir.

339
00:18:20,879 --> 00:18:22,380
Hmm, thank you.

340
00:18:31,681 --> 00:18:35,268
Hello there, civil servants. How are you doing?

341
00:18:35,477 --> 00:18:37,521
What's with that outfit, Ryotsu?

342
00:18:37,729 --> 00:18:42,108
These are blend clothes I ordered for three million yen.

343
00:18:42,317 --> 00:18:46,279
Sir, it's not "blend," but rather "brand" clothes.

344
00:18:48,198 --> 00:18:49,032
Sandayu!

345
00:18:49,241 --> 00:18:51,159
Please forgive my impertinence.

346
00:18:51,368 --> 00:18:52,494
Let me introduce him.

347
00:18:52,702 --> 00:18:55,789
This is Sato-kun who is my butler from today.

348
00:18:57,374 --> 00:19:00,627
I'm Sato. It's a privilege to make your acquaintance.

349
00:19:00,836 --> 00:19:02,379
Thank you. I'm Nakagawa.

350
00:19:02,587 --> 00:19:03,547
I'm Reiko.

351
00:19:03,755 --> 00:19:05,298
I'm Ohara, the senior officer here.

352
00:19:05,882 --> 00:19:09,553
Oh, I wanted to thank Nakagawa-kun and Reiko-kun for always helping me.

353
00:19:10,011 --> 00:19:11,930
It's a small amount, but please take it.

354
00:19:12,138 --> 00:19:13,306
This much?

355
00:19:13,515 --> 00:19:15,016
May I really take it?

356
00:19:15,225 --> 00:19:16,351
Absolutely.

357
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:19,938
R-Ryotsu, don't spend your money so freely!

358
00:19:20,146 --> 00:19:21,731
You must save it.

359
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:24,651
Sandayu, bring that thing to the chief.

360
00:19:24,859 --> 00:19:25,819
Yes, sir.

361
00:19:26,444 --> 00:19:27,404
What's that?

362
00:19:27,612 --> 00:19:31,032
I made you spend three million yen on parties the other day.

363
00:19:31,241 --> 00:19:33,451
Please keep this as my apology.

364
00:19:36,037 --> 00:19:38,707
Th-This much?

365
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:40,417
-May I? -Sure.

366
00:19:40,959 --> 00:19:42,878
Oh, let's do that thing.

367
00:19:43,086 --> 00:19:46,047
Sandayu, bring about 300 million yen into the back room.

368
00:19:46,256 --> 00:19:47,382
Yes, sir.

369
00:19:52,888 --> 00:19:54,472
-What's all this for? -W-Why?

370
00:20:00,061 --> 00:20:02,564
I always wanted to do this if I ever got rich.

371
00:20:04,566 --> 00:20:08,069
What a wonderful feeling! Why don't you join me, Chief?

372
00:20:08,278 --> 00:20:10,739
You idiot! I won't do it!

373
00:20:10,947 --> 00:20:12,073
He's gone money crazy.

374
00:20:12,949 --> 00:20:15,535
You'd better play with the cash while you can.

375
00:20:15,744 --> 00:20:17,287
While we can?

376
00:20:17,495 --> 00:20:20,081
Ryotsu, have you decided how to spend it?

377
00:20:20,290 --> 00:20:24,502
Sure, I ordered it on the day I won. It will arrive today.

378
00:20:26,004 --> 00:20:27,631
It's here!

379
00:20:27,839 --> 00:20:29,758
What did he order?

380
00:20:31,384 --> 00:20:33,345
Oh my gosh!

381
00:20:35,263 --> 00:20:38,516
He bought a real combat helicopter!

382
00:20:38,725 --> 00:20:40,018
And it's made of gold!

383
00:20:40,226 --> 00:20:43,647
No way! If it's real, it would cost over 10 billion yen!

384
00:20:45,690 --> 00:20:46,691
Surprised?

385
00:20:46,900 --> 00:20:48,735
Of course, I can't buy a real one.

386
00:20:48,944 --> 00:20:51,946
This is a 1:1 scale radio-controlled helicopter.

387
00:20:52,155 --> 00:20:55,367
It's realistic, custom-made, and gold-plated.

388
00:20:55,575 --> 00:20:57,911
It cost 5 billion yen!

389
00:20:58,119 --> 00:20:59,037
I'm getting a headache...

390
00:20:59,245 --> 00:21:00,288
Oh, Chief!

391
00:21:01,081 --> 00:21:02,040
Did you load the stuff?

392
00:21:02,248 --> 00:21:03,291
Yes, already.

393
00:21:04,376 --> 00:21:07,170
Okay, time to take it for a spin!

394
00:21:08,171 --> 00:21:10,715
Have a good flight, sir.

395
00:21:17,055 --> 00:21:18,765
Woo-hoo!

396
00:21:22,018 --> 00:21:23,645
It can really fly.

397
00:21:23,853 --> 00:21:25,855
What's he going to do?

398
00:21:26,398 --> 00:21:27,357
I feel great!

399
00:21:27,565 --> 00:21:29,776
It's just like flying in a real chopper!

400
00:21:30,193 --> 00:21:31,945
If I'm spending 5.5 billion yen,

401
00:21:32,153 --> 00:21:36,324
this is better for me than saving or donating it.

402
00:21:36,533 --> 00:21:39,828
Okay, let's scatter them over the park.

403
00:21:50,922 --> 00:21:52,966
Hello, ordinary citizens in town!

404
00:21:53,174 --> 00:21:58,138
I'm Kankichi Ryotsu, who won 5.5 billion yen in the lotto.

405
00:21:58,555 --> 00:22:02,225
It doesn't feel right to keep all my luck to myself,

406
00:22:02,434 --> 00:22:05,687
so I'll share it with you!

407
00:22:06,187 --> 00:22:08,273
Here I go! Take it!

408
00:22:08,898 --> 00:22:11,192
It's a lottery. What a grand idea.

409
00:22:11,401 --> 00:22:13,194
He's certainly giving away a lot.

410
00:22:13,403 --> 00:22:15,864
It's the 500 million yen left after buying the helicopter.

411
00:22:16,072 --> 00:22:17,866
500 million?

412
00:22:19,743 --> 00:22:21,453
Take it, everyone!

413
00:22:28,585 --> 00:22:31,296
Take this with you, too!

414
00:22:32,672 --> 00:22:34,924
This is such fun!

415
00:22:35,133 --> 00:22:37,260
Take this, too!

416
00:22:37,469 --> 00:22:40,221
And take this as well!

417
00:22:40,680 --> 00:22:41,556
&lt;i&gt;Eh?&lt;/i&gt;

418
00:22:43,266 --> 00:22:44,309
&lt;i&gt;Oops.&lt;/i&gt;

419
00:22:44,976 --> 00:22:47,145
&lt;i&gt;Oh, no!&lt;/i&gt;

420
00:22:48,772 --> 00:22:50,231
&lt;i&gt;That's my controller.&lt;/i&gt;

421
00:22:51,066 --> 00:22:54,778
&lt;i&gt;Without it, I can't fly!&lt;/i&gt;

422
00:23:03,953 --> 00:23:04,788
Ryo-chan!

423
00:23:04,996 --> 00:23:06,080
Are you okay?

424
00:23:08,792 --> 00:23:10,335
My chopper...

425
00:23:11,086 --> 00:23:13,755
My 5-billion-yen chopper's turned into ashes!

426
00:23:13,963 --> 00:23:16,758
Excuse me, what about my salary?

427
00:23:17,217 --> 00:23:19,010
You're in big trouble, Ryo-san!

428
00:23:19,219 --> 00:23:23,431
Lotto prize money is subject to a 30% federal tax in the U.S.!

429
00:23:23,640 --> 00:23:24,474
What?

430
00:23:24,682 --> 00:23:28,770
This letter says you must pay 30% of 5.5 billion yen in taxes.

431
00:23:28,978 --> 00:23:29,938
Huh?

432
00:23:30,522 --> 00:23:33,191
30% of 5.5 billion yen?

433
00:23:33,399 --> 00:23:35,652
What? That's 1.65 billion yen!

434
00:23:36,069 --> 00:23:37,153
Oof...

435
00:23:42,909 --> 00:23:45,161
After getting 5.5 billion yen,

436
00:23:45,537 --> 00:23:47,372
he spent all of it in no time.

437
00:23:47,580 --> 00:23:53,378
And ended up 1.65 billion yen in debt.

438
00:23:53,586 --> 00:23:55,964
He's the definition of an idiot.

439
00:23:56,172 --> 00:23:58,424
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

440
00:23:58,633 --> 00:24:02,053
1.65 BILLION YEN

441
00:24:05,223 --> 00:24:07,559
&lt;i&gt;Come on in, take a look!&lt;/i&gt;

442
00:24:07,767 --> 00:24:10,270
&lt;i&gt;It snows in Kameari in mid-summer!&lt;/i&gt;

443
00:24:10,478 --> 00:24:12,147
&lt;i&gt;Shaved ice on a hot day!&lt;/i&gt;

444
00:24:12,355 --> 00:24:13,940
&lt;i&gt;Directly imported from Alaska.&lt;/i&gt;

445
00:24:14,482 --> 00:24:16,943
&lt;i&gt;How about some special&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;super-size shaved ice?&lt;/i&gt;

446
00:24:17,151 --> 00:24:20,238
NEXT EPISODE I SCREAM FOR SHAVED ICE SKIING!

447
00:24:20,446 --> 00:24:21,614
&lt;i&gt;Don't miss it!&lt;/i&gt;

448
00:24:32,917 --> 00:24:37,172
&lt;i&gt;Let's keep smiling always&lt;/i&gt;

449
00:24:37,839 --> 00:24:41,467
&lt;i&gt;Even when things go wrong&lt;/i&gt;

450
00:24:41,676 --> 00:24:45,930
&lt;i&gt;Keep a pretty smile on your face&lt;/i&gt;

451
00:24:46,556 --> 00:24:50,977
&lt;i&gt;And go out as if nothing happened&lt;/i&gt;

452
00:24:51,519 --> 00:24:55,064
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

453
00:24:55,273 --> 00:24:59,235
&lt;i&gt;You did nothing wrong&lt;/i&gt;

454
00:25:00,195 --> 00:25:03,740
&lt;i&gt;Hey, show me your smile&lt;/i&gt;

455
00:25:03,948 --> 00:25:07,368
&lt;i&gt;Just like you did before, yeah&lt;/i&gt;

456
00:25:07,869 --> 00:25:12,040
&lt;i&gt;I want you to smile always&lt;/i&gt;

457
00:25:12,749 --> 00:25:17,212
&lt;i&gt;A woman with a frown isn't pretty&lt;/i&gt;

458
00:25:17,712 --> 00:25:23,259
&lt;i&gt;So you should smile as soon as you can&lt;/i&gt;

459
00:25:24,052 --> 00:25:26,971
&lt;i&gt;It's the grown-up thing to do&lt;/i&gt;

460
00:25:39,150 --> 00:25:43,863
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
